chore(deploy): land M6 release & deploy infrastructure (Dockerfile + Helm + compose + signed images)

* Multi-arch container image: rewrite the legacy single-stage Dockerfile
  into a four-stage cargo-chef pipeline (chef -> planner -> builder ->
  runtime). The builder accepts a `FEATURES` build arg so the same
  Dockerfile produces both the lean HTTP-only image and a TLS+OTel
  build, picks up the new workspace layout, ships under
  `gcr.io/distroless/cc-debian12:nonroot`, exposes /etc/corx/config.toml
  with sensible env defaults, and ENTRYPOINTs into `corx serve`.
* `.dockerignore` removes target/, charts/, docs/ and the .git tree from
  the build context so cargo-chef's recipe stays stable across feature
  branches.
* `docker-compose.yml` plus `deploy/{prometheus.yml, otel-collector.yaml,
  grafana-datasources.yml}` give a one-shot local stack: corx + OTLP
  collector + Prometheus + Grafana wired together with a healthcheck
  that re-uses the new `corx check` subcommand.
* New Helm chart at `charts/corx`: ConfigMap-mounted TOML, Deployment
  with checksum-based config rollout, Service, Ingress, HPA, PDB,
  ServiceAccount, ServiceMonitor and a NOTES.txt that documents the
  SIGHUP-driven hot-reload contract. Probes target `/livez` and
  `/readyz` to align with the M3 readiness model.
* New GitHub workflows:
  - `docker.yml` builds linux/amd64 + linux/arm64 images, pushes to
    GHCR, signs each tag with cosign, generates a CycloneDX SBOM via
    anchore/sbom-action, and attests provenance for tagged releases via
    `actions/attest-build-provenance`.
  - `helm.yml` lints, renders and `kubeconform`-validates the chart on
    every PR, then publishes a packaged chart to GHCR's OCI registry on
    tag pushes.
* `deny.toml` codifies the cargo-deny policy used by the upstream
  `qntx/workflows/ci-rust.yml` runner -- explicit licence allow-list,
  yanked-deny, registry pinning to crates.io.
